---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import { NOTES } from '../../config';

const note = NOTES.find((n) => n.id === 'computer-networks');
const buy = note?.buyUrl ?? '/notes';
const price = note?.price ?? '₹49';
const pages = note?.pages ?? 20;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Preview: Computer networks"
  description="A free sample of the networks note. Two machines, four facts, then the tuple. The PDF has the rest."
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Preview" title="Computer networks, as they show up on a box">
    <p class="hero-dek">
      A free sample. The PDF is {pages} pages.
    </p>
  </PageHero>

  <article class="sample">
    <p class="lede">
      One program on one computer is trying to send bytes to a program on
      another computer. Everything in these notes is how that arrow works, or
      fails.
    </p>

    <h2>The picture</h2>
    <p>
      Left: a process on your laptop. Right: a process on another machine. The
      arrow is packets, each carrying to this IP, this port. Layer names later
      have somewhere to sit if you keep this picture.
    </p>
    <figure>
      <img
        src="/notes/net-preview-machines.svg"
        alt="A client process sending packets to a server process at an IP and port."
        width="720"
        height="280"
      />
      <figcaption>Figure. The whole subject in one picture.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h2>Four facts</h2>
    <p>
      If a connect fails and you cannot point at one of these four, stop and
      name them on paper before you capture packets.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Address.</strong> Which machine. Almost always an IP.</li>
      <li><strong>Door.</strong> Which process. That is a port.</li>
      <li><strong>Path.</strong> What sits between: NAT, a filter, a hop.</li>
      <li><strong>Talk.</strong> TCP (an agreement) or UDP (a throw).</li>
    </ul>
    <figure>
      <img
        src="/notes/net-preview-facts.svg"
        alt="Four boxes: address, door, path, talk."
        width="720"
        height="260"
      />
      <figcaption>Figure. If you cannot name these four, you are guessing.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <blockquote>
      A TCP connection is source IP, source port, dest IP, dest port. Dest port
      443 is shared. The conversation is the row.
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      That is the sample. The PDF walks ping versus 443, NAT, localhost, HTTP
      last, and the questions I want answered in a room.
    </p>

    <div class="cta">
      <p>The rest is in the file.</p>
      <a class="buy" href={buy}>Buy the PDF, {price}</a>
      <a class="back" href="/notes">All notes</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero-dek {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin: 1.2rem 0 0;
  }
  /* The shell, not the prose measure: the sample figures are drawn on a 720px
     canvas and the text is meant to run the same width as them, the way it does
     on a phone. */
  .sample {
    max-width: var(--shell);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: 2.5rem var(--gutter) 5rem;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
  }
  .sample h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 2.2rem 0 0.7rem;
  }
  .sample p,
  .sample li {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .sample ul {
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
  }
  .sample blockquote {
    margin: 1.2rem 0;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    background: var(--paper-tint);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .sample figure {
    margin: 1.4rem 0 1.8rem;
  }
  .sample img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    background: var(--paper-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .sample figcaption {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .cta {
    margin-top: 2.8rem;
    padding-top: 1.6rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .cta p {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .buy {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--paper);
    background: var(--accent);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 2px;
    padding: 0.48rem 0.95rem;
    margin-right: 0.75rem;
  }
  .buy:hover {
    background: var(--accent-warm);
    border-color: var(--accent-warm);
  }
  .back {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
